  "id": "Compound::DB01327 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Cefazolin, a cephalosporin antibiotic, is linked to Slc22a6 through a shared pathway involving Cephalosporins and Ceftriaxone. The evidence suggests that Cefazolin, as part of the broader Cephalosporin class, binds to Slc22a6 via Ceftriaxone, which is a direct interaction. This relationship is supported by the lowest common ancestor (LCA) structure, where Cefazolin and Ceftriaxone share a common ancestor in the Cephalosporin category. The causal link between Cefazolin and Serum Sickness-like Reaction, which is then associated with Ceftriaxone, further reinforces the indirect connection to Slc22a6. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism where the antibiotic Cefazolin, through its inclusion in the Cephalosporin class, indirectly influences Slc22a6 via Ceftriaxone. The evidence suggests a dependence on the antibiotic class for the interaction with Slc22a6, emphasizing the role of the Cephalosporin family in mediating this biological relationship.",
